-   <xref target="RFC7344" section="1" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7344#section-1" derivedContent="RFC7344"/>.1) Earlier, &quot;parent name server&quot; was defined
-   in <xref target="RFC0882" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC0882"/> as &quot;the name server that has authority over the place
-   in the domain name space that will hold the new domain&quot;.  (Note
-   that <xref target="RFC0882" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC0882"/> was obsoleted by <xref target="RFC1034" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1034"/> and <xref target="RFC1035" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1035"/>.)
